1
00:00:05,679 --> 00:00:08,759
Rare Ghost Flower Discovered
Deep in the Great Snow Mountain.

2
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:11,118
Legend has it that this flower
blooms at the gates of hell.

3
00:00:11,119 --> 00:00:14,400
Anyone who sees it can have their
soul pass through it into the underworld.

4
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:15,720
It's fake.

5
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,280
What?

6
00:00:17,359 --> 00:00:19,679
I'm saying the content
in this video is totally fake.

7
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,280
The Ghost Flower isn't that mystical.

8
00:00:21,519 --> 00:00:22,959
Changyang explained it to me before.

9
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:25,718
It's rare not because it has
anything to do with the underworld,

10
00:00:25,719 --> 00:00:28,760
but because it only grows in
pristine ecological environments.

11
00:00:30,719 --> 00:00:32,296
I remember Changyang took a picture of it.

12
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:33,719
I thought he photoshopped it.

13
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:37,200
Is it really as beautiful
as it is in the video?

14
00:00:37,679 --> 00:00:39,079
It looks even better in person.

15
00:00:39,719 --> 00:00:41,279
When I first saw it,

16
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:42,520
I was thrilled for days.

17
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:45,719
Its crystal-clear purity

18
00:00:46,159 --> 00:00:48,399
is like a transparent bar of soap.

19
00:00:48,719 --> 00:00:51,719
It can wash away all the dust in
your heart, leaving it completely clean.

20
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:53,520
It's truly magical.

21
00:00:53,799 --> 00:00:56,920
It feels like it can actually
bring a person's soul back to life.

22
00:00:57,079 --> 00:00:59,239
I'll look for it for you when
I go into the mountains.

23
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:00,359
Changyang taught me everything.

24
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,880
I know roughly where to find it.

25
00:01:03,079 --> 00:01:06,958
It's a pity that when I went
into the mountains back then,

26
00:01:06,959 --> 00:01:08,359
I couldn't capture it on camera.

27
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:12,280
But a photo definitely can't compare
to seeing it with your own eyes.

28
00:01:24,519 --> 00:01:25,799
Let's do a jump shot.

29
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:27,000
Ready.

30
00:01:27,001 --> 00:01:29,000
Three, two, one, yay!

31
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:31,439
Wow, this one looks great.

32
00:01:31,719 --> 00:01:32,599
Let me see.

33
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,000
Let me take one of you two.

34
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,599
Oh man, you guys are so cheesy.

35
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,439
What kind of tourist
photo is this? Make a heart.

36
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,319
Like this.

37
00:01:44,439 --> 00:01:45,040
How's that?

38
00:01:45,239 --> 00:01:46,719
Can you guys show a little chemistry?

39
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,040
How about this?

40
00:01:49,599 --> 00:01:50,599
Hold on.

41
00:01:52,519 --> 00:01:53,959
You blinked. Let's take another one.

42
00:01:58,519 --> 00:01:59,439
Ah, the framing is off.

43
00:01:59,439 --> 00:02:00,879
One more.

44
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,479
Not bad.
Looks good.

45
00:02:10,001 --> 00:02:11,041
Two hearts beating as one.

46
00:02:11,319 --> 00:02:13,240
Let's take one with the three of us.

47
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:13,680
Ah.
Sure.

48
00:02:17,879 --> 00:02:18,879
Director Jiang.

49
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,319
I'll take it.

50
00:02:22,199 --> 00:02:24,039
Three, two, one.

51
00:02:24,319 --> 00:02:27,000
Great Snow Mountain, here we come!

52
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:43,500
"A Winter Sun Wakes the Wind in Spring Hills' Dream"

53
00:02:47,293 --> 00:02:51,093
(Episode 13: The Pure Land)

54
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,615
We've been shooting all
day and it's just you two.

55
00:02:54,639 --> 00:02:56,959
Now you know the importance
of professional actors, right?

56
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,319
Brother, did you take on a new role?

57
00:02:59,719 --> 00:03:00,719
No, I didn't.

58
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:03,120
You look like you're experiencing
the life of a tough guy.

59
00:03:04,599 --> 00:03:06,559
Are you going to eat
that? If not, give it to me.

60
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:10,840
You eat some too.

61
00:03:17,719 --> 00:03:18,719
Lang Di!

62
00:03:19,599 --> 00:03:21,280
Can I get a picture with you?

63
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,400
Lang Di, can we take a photo together?

64
00:03:23,479 --> 00:03:24,639
Ah, let's go over there.

65
00:03:24,919 --> 00:03:26,719
Ah, okay, sure.

66
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,840
Afraid the fans might misunderstand.

67
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:30,240
I know.

68
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:49,918
Brother, right now you look
exactly like a hairy mountain monkey

69
00:03:49,919 --> 00:03:51,376
getting grabbed by tourists for photos.

70
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,400
Just eat your food.

71
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,400
Director Jiang.

72
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,680
I checked the route this morning.

73
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,918
Brother Wenshu, you haven't had the tea
from Great Snow Mountain yet, have you?

74
00:04:09,919 --> 00:04:11,199
We can just bypass this section.

75
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:12,816
They're doing roadwork here right now.

76
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,039
Is there any difference?

77
00:04:15,439 --> 00:04:16,919
It's mellower and clearer than Molie.

78
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,399
And lighter than Xi Gui.

79
00:04:18,519 --> 00:04:19,199
Yeah.

80
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,638
Molie has a commanding presence,

81
00:04:20,639 --> 00:04:21,758
much like Changyang.

82
00:04:21,759 --> 00:04:24,199
Xi Gui has an enchanting
floral scent, like my brother.

83
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,040
Great Snow Mountain is like you.

84
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,160
Hmm.

85
00:04:33,199 --> 00:04:35,398
I've always felt I don't
have any distinct traits.

86
00:04:35,399 --> 00:04:35,800
Hmm.

87
00:04:35,801 --> 00:04:37,838
From a director's casting perspective,

88
00:04:37,839 --> 00:04:39,279
it's called lacking recognizability.

89
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,959
Then do you think I'm recognizable?

90
00:04:45,279 --> 00:04:46,680
Let me think about it carefully.

91
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,639
There's a saying in the tea mountains:

92
00:04:51,959 --> 00:04:53,439
"To reach Great Snow Mountain,

93
00:04:53,639 --> 00:04:54,879
one must pass through Dongguo."

94
00:04:55,079 --> 00:04:56,839
The flavor of Dongguo
tea is quite like you.

95
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:00,239
It's the place we went to a few days ago.

96
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:03,399
Yeah. You only understand it
once you've walked through it.

97
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,399
We've arrived at Great Snow Mountain.

98
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,160
I've been thinking all day and still
don't know how to bring it up to Qingtian.

99
00:05:18,079 --> 00:05:19,680
I'm out of ideas.

100
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,879
I can only wait for your reply.

101
00:05:23,279 --> 00:05:26,879
I'm sure you'll come up with a
good solution. I believe in you.

102
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,160
Love you.

103
00:05:36,879 --> 00:05:37,879
What are you doing?

104
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:39,976
Since you're here, of
course I'm staying with you.

105
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,639
You're my actual brother.

106
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,600
Tian.

107
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:09,360
If one day I die,

108
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,759
I mean, hypothetically.

109
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,800
Death is a clean break.

110
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:14,360
A clean break?
How is it clean?

111
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,880
Being dead is truly
cleaner than being alive.

112
00:06:17,759 --> 00:06:18,959
Think about it carefully.

113
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,800
In death, you return to the earth,

114
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,040
back to the soil.

115
00:06:23,639 --> 00:06:25,759
And the soil nurtures new life.

116
00:06:26,279 --> 00:06:28,199
That dark, muddy dirt

117
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,560
is much cleaner and
purer than the human heart.

118
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:57,759
Brother, how did you know for
sure that you love Changyang?

119
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,600
I could never say the
cruelest things to him.

120
00:07:01,839 --> 00:07:03,479
What kind of things are considered cruel?

121
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:06,599
"Breaking up makes life easier."

122
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,600
"Death is a clean break."

123
00:07:10,199 --> 00:07:11,360
What about him towards you?

124
00:07:12,959 --> 00:07:13,959
The same.

125
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,880
Anyway, neither of us would ever want to
leave the other just to make life easier.

126
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:26,199
What if Changyang died?

127
00:07:28,839 --> 00:07:29,759
I'd hook up with a sugar daddy

128
00:07:29,839 --> 00:07:31,439
and live out my twilight years in peace.

129
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,800
Are you serious?

130
00:07:34,439 --> 00:07:35,480
Who knows?

131
00:07:37,079 --> 00:07:39,319
In life, you have to be
open-minded and learn to let go.

132
00:07:40,959 --> 00:07:42,639
We can't even control ourselves,

133
00:07:43,079 --> 00:07:44,360
let alone others.

134
00:08:09,839 --> 00:08:12,079
Tian, which direction
is that ancient tea tree?

135
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,839
Follow me this way.

136
00:08:15,959 --> 00:08:16,959
Okay, coming.

137
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:23,240
He already knew.

138
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,480
I noticed a long time ago.

139
00:08:27,199 --> 00:08:30,480
I had the caregiver record
Chen Zhu's final moments.

140
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,440
I wanted to leave Qingtian
something to remember him by.

141
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:41,000
You probably don't know how
his parents treated Qingtian.

142
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:44,000
I can imagine.

143
00:08:44,159 --> 00:08:46,176
Isn't that how it always plays
out in those short dramas?

144
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,920
It's even more exaggerated than the dramas.

145
00:08:49,159 --> 00:08:50,679
Whenever I think about how they acted,

146
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:54,759
I often feel a surge of hatred.

147
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,440
I'd think to myself, "Your son
deserved to be in that car crash."

148
00:08:59,039 --> 00:09:00,240
That doesn't sound like you.

149
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,480
I'm only human.

150
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:11,200
Changyang and I have
been down both paths before.

151
00:09:12,279 --> 00:09:14,559
The eastern path leads to
the thousand-year-old tea tree.

152
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,360
You can stand right
at the base of the tree.

153
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:18,799
The western path leads to a ridge

154
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:20,400
where you can see all of the tea trees.

155
00:09:21,279 --> 00:09:23,798
Director Jiang, if you want
to shoot from both sides,

156
00:09:23,799 --> 00:09:24,936
we'll have to come back again tomorrow.

157
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:25,960
Sure, no problem.

158
00:09:26,159 --> 00:09:27,159
Let's go.

159
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,360
Coming.

160
00:09:32,159 --> 00:09:33,799
Slow down, Qingtian.

161
00:09:35,039 --> 00:09:36,279
You guys keep up.

162
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:59,039
The market has shrunk severely.

163
00:09:59,559 --> 00:10:01,879
Project cycles are long,
and returns are slow.

164
00:10:02,639 --> 00:10:03,999
Our project team still needs to provide

165
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,760
the direction discussed
in the last meeting.

166
00:10:05,785 --> 00:10:09,226
We'll cut the originally planned fantasy
drama, Canghuang Yin, into a short drama.

167
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,000
We'll shoot it as an episodic story.

168
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,360
We'll call it "The Male Queen is a Dragon."

169
00:10:17,159 --> 00:10:19,039
I admit it's tacky and cliché,

170
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,399
but it fits the current market environment.

171
00:10:21,559 --> 00:10:22,798
If we shoot it in vertical format,

172
00:10:22,799 --> 00:10:23,919
the cost will be even lower.

173
00:10:25,759 --> 00:10:26,759
Come in.

174
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,480
Sorry to interrupt, Producer Yang.

175
00:10:30,559 --> 00:10:31,798
I urgently need some
stills from South Tower.

176
00:10:31,799 --> 00:10:32,600
Please send them to me quickly.
Okay, give me ten minutes.

177
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:34,399
We're almost done here.
Okay.

178
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:40,600
Boss Fang insists that art must
come after putting food on the table.

179
00:10:40,679 --> 00:10:42,960
Our company hasn't
had a single failure so far.

180
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,640
We've been preparing
Canghuang Yin for over a year.

181
00:10:45,799 --> 00:10:48,200
Everyone knows exactly
why it hasn't been greenlit.

182
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:49,679
We can't afford to lose.

183
00:10:50,159 --> 00:10:53,279
In the film and television industry,
one failure equals a loss of credibility.

184
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
But everyone,

185
00:10:56,039 --> 00:10:57,840
we aren't lacking startup capital.

186
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,879
What we lack is confidence in the market.

187
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,720
We lack the conviction that this
project will definitely make money.

188
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,200
Come in.

189
00:11:09,279 --> 00:11:10,279
Producer.

190
00:11:10,639 --> 00:11:11,639
Where are the stills?

191
00:11:11,679 --> 00:11:13,439
Oh, right, I'll get them
for you right away.

192
00:11:15,799 --> 00:11:17,960
Were you guys just
discussing that fantasy drama?

193
00:11:19,417 --> 00:11:21,775
If we make the content too high-brow,

194
00:11:21,799 --> 00:11:23,119
the audience won't understand it.

195
00:11:23,279 --> 00:11:24,639
If we make it too low-brow,

196
00:11:24,679 --> 00:11:26,200
we can't accept it ourselves.

197
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:27,240
Producer Yang.
It's a dilemma.

198
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:29,600
Send me a copy of those stills later.

199
00:11:29,759 --> 00:11:30,759
I need to take a call.

200
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Alright, go ahead.
Okay.

201
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:38,853
Skipping dinner? Dieting?

202
00:11:39,516 --> 00:11:40,536
You're not fat.

203
00:11:43,159 --> 00:11:45,279
I heard your company has
a big project coming up.

204
00:11:45,399 --> 00:11:46,479
The premise is pretty good.

205
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,759
It's not for me.

206
00:11:50,399 --> 00:11:52,480
Han Lu, you're very smart.

207
00:11:52,639 --> 00:11:54,840
But sometimes it pays to play dumb.

208
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,600
Whether I'm smart or dumb,

209
00:11:58,759 --> 00:11:59,879
I'm just an ant.

210
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:03,799
But I think it's exactly
because ants are so small

211
00:12:04,039 --> 00:12:05,359
that they aren't afraid of death.

212
00:12:05,799 --> 00:12:07,159
They're too small.

213
00:12:07,399 --> 00:12:09,480
No one cares if they live or die.

214
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,400
They live insignificant lives,

215
00:12:11,759 --> 00:12:13,000
and die a quick death.

216
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,360
But people are different.

217
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:19,000
Especially the ones who can step on them.

218
00:12:22,879 --> 00:12:23,960
Follow me,

219
00:12:24,159 --> 00:12:25,759
and I'll make you a top star.

220
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,360
You'll have whatever you want.

221
00:12:28,039 --> 00:12:30,456
Mr. Jin, you still don't quite
understand the entertainment industry.

222
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:32,360
Top stars are never just handed their fame.

223
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:41,440
Tell me,

224
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:43,399
what do you want?

225
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,480
I don't want anything.

226
00:12:48,159 --> 00:12:49,159
Welcome home, wifey.

227
00:12:49,759 --> 00:12:51,039
You've been pretty free lately.

228
00:12:51,679 --> 00:12:53,336
I turned down a few
roles. Too lazy to shoot.

229
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:54,799
Come try my new dish.

230
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:56,200
Coming.

231
00:12:58,159 --> 00:13:00,799
Ever since you figured
out how much salt to use,

232
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,840
you seem to be obsessed with cooking.

233
00:13:04,019 --> 00:13:05,779
- Of course.
- Give me a kiss.

234
00:13:08,279 --> 00:13:10,279
It's way better than
shooting those crappy movies.

235
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,959
I don't have to suck up to producers,

236
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:13,799
or deal with those idiot directors.

237
00:13:14,399 --> 00:13:15,799
I just need your nod of approval.

238
00:13:17,799 --> 00:13:18,799
Here.

239
00:13:20,159 --> 00:13:22,080
If we keep eating like this,

240
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:25,440
we'll be kicked out of the
idol race in less than two years.

241
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:27,799
Hurry up and try the new dish I learned.

242
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:31,039
Today... well, earlier,

243
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:32,479
that short drama director
reached out to me again.

244
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,999
He wants me to be the
male lead in his next project.

245
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,200
Guess how I replied.

246
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:38,759
The one who spends eight
hours shooting actresses,

247
00:13:38,799 --> 00:13:40,839
and does one take for
actors? That old geezer?

248
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:41,600
Yeah, that's him.
You still remember him?

249
00:13:42,879 --> 00:13:43,999
How could I forget?

250
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,600
Didn't you tell me about him before?

251
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,840
He films actresses from head to toe.

252
00:13:50,679 --> 00:13:52,360
You have no idea. When we were shooting,

253
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,159
he'd film a mouth and say,

254
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:55,879
"Come on, part your lips a bit."

255
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,440
"Yeah, a little more, a little more."

256
00:13:57,480 --> 00:13:59,200
"Tilt your neck up a bit more, a bit more."

257
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,240
For one bed scene,

258
00:14:00,279 --> 00:14:01,599
just a close-up of the actress,

259
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:03,240
he wanted to shoot 800 different angles.

260
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,440
Fuck, it was like shooting a softcore porn.

261
00:14:06,559 --> 00:14:07,559
Show a little class.

262
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:10,399
Hurry up and guess what I told him.

263
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:12,600
Let me think.

264
00:14:15,159 --> 00:14:17,279
You told him, "Director,

265
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,960
you shoot really well,

266
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:20,638
but after I put clips from our show

267
00:14:20,639 --> 00:14:22,200
into my portfolio,

268
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:24,360
a lot of directors were
too scared to cast me.

269
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:26,480
They said my acting was too over the top.

270
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,480
If I take another role of yours,

271
00:14:28,679 --> 00:14:30,080
my career will be over."

272
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:33,439
Wow, how are you even more savage than me?

273
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,599
I should've waited for you to come back

274
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,639
and had you reply for me.

275
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,840
So how did you actually reply?

276
00:14:40,399 --> 00:14:42,600
I said, "Director,

277
00:14:42,799 --> 00:14:45,039
I really don't think
your shows need actors.

278
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:46,239
Just cast all actresses.

279
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:47,360
Or have them cross-dress,

280
00:14:47,399 --> 00:14:48,878
and just deepfake the faces in post."

281
00:14:48,879 --> 00:14:51,679
"Imagine how much fun
you'd have filming that."

282
00:14:51,879 --> 00:14:53,480
You're clearly way more savage than me.

283
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:56,759
If we end up offending the
entire entertainment industry,

284
00:14:56,799 --> 00:14:58,080
what are we gonna do?

285
00:14:58,799 --> 00:15:00,959
We'll quit. I'll open a restaurant,

286
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,120
and you can be an influencer.

287
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,640
We'll run an influencer restaurant.

288
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,600
Then you still need more practice.

289
00:15:07,159 --> 00:15:08,399
Is it not good?

290
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,039
Is Tian here?

291
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,279
He didn't look for you?

292
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:30,000
Didn't he say you needed him for some ADR?

293
00:15:30,759 --> 00:15:32,439
I've been waiting for him this whole time.

294
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:43,480
Is Tian with you?
No.

295
00:15:53,879 --> 00:15:54,879
Qingtian!

296
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,600
Qingtian!

297
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:05,960
Qingtian!

298
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,240
Qingtian!

299
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Qingtian!

300
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:15,960
Is Qingtian here?
No.

301
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:21,480
Qingtian!

302
00:16:35,159 --> 00:16:36,360
Go look over there.

303
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:38,080
You go that way.

304
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:46,080
Qingtian!

305
00:16:50,799 --> 00:16:51,879
What are you two doing?

306
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:04,000
Where did you go?

307
00:17:06,039 --> 00:17:08,000
If you want to die,
wait until I'm dead first!

308
00:17:09,759 --> 00:17:11,000
Feng Qinglang, are you crazy?

309
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:13,759
I'm crazy? Which one of us is crazy?

310
00:17:14,039 --> 00:17:16,160
You've been hung up on
a vegetable for four years!

311
00:17:16,599 --> 00:17:17,839
You've made yourself depressed!

312
00:17:18,039 --> 00:17:19,479
Running off in the middle of the
night where no one can find you!

313
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:20,520
What are you trying to do?

314
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:23,199
Do you want to die?

315
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,039
I'll give you a knife!
For a dead guy...

316
00:17:24,759 --> 00:17:25,759
Do you want to die?

317
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:30,599
Qingtian, it's time to wake up.

318
00:17:30,839 --> 00:17:32,599
Chen Zhu's death has
nothing to do with you.

319
00:17:32,759 --> 00:17:34,599
But his car accident does!

320
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:39,200
Did you drive the car that hit him?

321
00:17:39,839 --> 00:17:41,640
Did he die under your wheels?

322
00:17:41,759 --> 00:17:43,079
He was calling me!

323
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:45,080
He came out to his family because of me!

324
00:17:46,599 --> 00:17:50,240
Yes! It's me! I'm the murderer!

325
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:52,960
I killed him!

326
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,640
I killed him!

327
00:17:55,559 --> 00:17:56,880
And he killed me too!

328
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:00,839
He killed me too!

329
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,880
He killed me too!

330
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,799
He killed me too!

331
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,598
He killed me too!

332
00:18:12,599 --> 00:18:13,758
Alright.

333
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:15,000
Just let it all out.

334
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:16,759
Listen to me.

335
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,839
Neither of you owes the other anything.

336
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,200
You're even.

337
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,479
He went up to the sky

338
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:30,480
and became a star.

339
00:18:32,759 --> 00:18:34,039
You're still here on earth.

340
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:39,279
When you miss him, just look up at the sky.

341
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:04,359
You know how to comfort people now.

342
00:19:05,799 --> 00:19:07,160
I had a good teacher.

343
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,640
Director Jiang wants to
record the sound of picking tea.

344
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,599
I went out to find a tea needle.

345
00:19:19,079 --> 00:19:20,079
I know.

346
00:19:20,839 --> 00:19:22,240
I just got the acting bug.

347
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,160
I've never seen you
act this well on screen.

348
00:19:26,079 --> 00:19:27,759
Still not as good as you.

349
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:29,560
Hiding it for so many years.

350
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,440
If I hadn't yelled at you,

351
00:19:31,599 --> 00:19:33,319
how long were you going to keep pretending?

352
00:19:34,559 --> 00:19:36,160
Until I became a star too.

353
00:19:37,359 --> 00:19:38,400
That's easy.

354
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,400
I'll send you to a primeval forest,

355
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:41,920
and you'll grow fur in a month.

356
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,240
A hairy ape.

357
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:54,160
Bro.

358
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:56,480
Love you.

359
00:19:59,279 --> 00:20:00,400
I don't need your love.

360
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,240
I've got someone.

361
00:20:05,279 --> 00:20:07,000
Your someone isn't around.

362
00:20:13,599 --> 00:20:15,079
The little crybaby is back.

363
00:20:28,079 --> 00:20:29,079
Hand it over.

364
00:20:29,839 --> 00:20:30,759
Look at that smile.

365
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:32,040
You're grinning from ear to ear.

366
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:33,200
Give it to me.

367
00:20:36,039 --> 00:20:37,480
How do you know who it is?

368
00:20:38,759 --> 00:20:41,079
Wouldn't I know how
many seeds I've planted?

369
00:20:49,359 --> 00:20:49,960
Bring it here.
Hello.

370
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:52,959
The number you dialed is not answering.

371
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,758
We will transfer you to voicemail.

372
00:20:54,759 --> 00:20:56,400
Please leave a message after the beep.

373
00:20:56,599 --> 00:20:59,759
Damn kid. Go play with the guy next door.

374
00:21:00,079 --> 00:21:01,079
Go.

375
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:24,359
If I told you I only had five minutes,

376
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:26,880
how much longer would you wait to speak?

377
00:21:30,279 --> 00:21:33,200
Brother Wenshu, my brother told
me to go play with the guy next door.

378
00:21:33,759 --> 00:21:35,400
I didn't have time to read your message.

379
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:37,616
That brat Qingtian wasted
three minutes of my time.

380
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:38,839
He's on the phone, right?

381
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:40,640
You even guessed that?

382
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,400
The soundproofing here is terrible.

383
00:21:55,759 --> 00:21:57,799
You go do your thing, I'll play by myself.

384
00:21:58,599 --> 00:21:59,480
Two minutes left.
What do you want to hear?

385
00:22:00,559 --> 00:22:02,000
I'll say whatever you want to hear.

386
00:22:02,839 --> 00:22:04,000
I want to hear...

387
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,160
Speak faster.

388
00:22:06,359 --> 00:22:07,400
We don't have much time.

389
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:09,015
I want to hear you set off firecrackers.

390
00:22:09,039 --> 00:22:10,240
Popping endlessly.

391
00:22:16,039 --> 00:22:18,680
Whatever you want to play, I'll join you.

392
00:22:31,039 --> 00:22:32,079
Qingtian is fine now.

393
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:33,360
I gave him the third degree.

394
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:34,559
It worked pretty well.

395
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:37,559
Last time you left,
I forgot to ask you.

396
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:40,216
Do you still have any vacation days left?

397
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:41,520
You didn't go back to Shangjing,

398
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,399
and stayed in the
mountains for half a month,

399
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,599
just to wait for this?

400
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:45,839
If you have time off,

401
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:47,599
I could rush over since it's close by.

402
00:22:48,559 --> 00:22:49,679
If I went back to Shangjing,

403
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:51,840
I'd never be able to fly back here.

404
00:22:52,359 --> 00:22:55,559
So, should I say I have time off or not?

405
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:58,160
You really do?

406
00:22:58,839 --> 00:23:01,640
Mr. Big Star, act like
you're worth a bit more.

407
00:23:02,799 --> 00:23:04,439
I'm selling myself short in front of you.

408
00:23:04,839 --> 00:23:06,480
I'm selling myself short in front of you.

409
00:23:21,759 --> 00:23:22,640
Send me your location.

410
00:23:22,641 --> 00:23:23,759
I'll drive over.

411
00:23:24,359 --> 00:23:25,480
I'm not sending it tonight.

412
00:23:25,759 --> 00:23:27,160
I won't let you drive at night.

413
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,400
Fine.

414
00:23:30,279 --> 00:23:32,440
Then send it to me at
exactly 6:00 AM tomorrow.

415
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:39,240
That day I sneaked out to cry,

416
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:42,160
you saw me, didn't you?

417
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:44,400
Yeah.

418
00:23:46,799 --> 00:23:47,799
Brother Wenshu,

419
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:52,039
thank you for always watching over me.

420
00:23:54,759 --> 00:23:56,479
I was afraid something might happen to you,

421
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:59,640
so I kept following you.

422
00:24:01,880 --> 00:24:04,079
I'm talking about that
time at the hospital.

423
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:07,559
You went to see Brother Chen Zhu.

424
00:24:09,039 --> 00:24:12,880
Thank you for watching over me since then.

425
00:24:18,279 --> 00:24:21,759
I remember you were the one who
helped me find the Ghost Flower.

426
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:32,640
Brother Wenshu,

427
00:24:34,599 --> 00:24:38,680
wait for me to get myself together.

428
00:25:04,359 --> 00:25:06,726
[The Classic of Tea]

429
00:25:18,960 --> 00:25:20,160
You're up so early.

430
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:24,640
Go back to sleep.

431
00:26:57,640 --> 00:27:00,200
Tiantian, look where Grandma is.

432
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:04,200
Grandma has already climbed to the
top of the mountain to watch the sunrise.

433
00:27:04,839 --> 00:27:06,598
I've already sent it to your mom.

434
00:27:06,599 --> 00:27:07,679
And in a little while,

435
00:27:07,680 --> 00:27:09,160
I'll send it to your brother.

436
00:27:10,160 --> 00:27:11,758
My brother can see the sunrise too.

437
00:27:11,759 --> 00:27:12,759
He went out.

438
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:15,759
Then what is your brother doing?

439
00:27:16,473 --> 00:27:17,793
Qinglang is out meeting his beau.

440
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:21,480
Got it. Haha.

441
00:27:27,799 --> 00:27:29,640
Alright, Grandma is hanging up now.

442
00:27:29,880 --> 00:27:30,880
Bye-bye.

443
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:32,160
Bye-bye.

444
00:27:38,559 --> 00:27:40,535
What's dangerous? A bunch
of my brothers are here.

445
00:27:40,559 --> 00:27:41,639
Brother Wenshu is here too.

446
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:43,400
Qingtian.

447
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:44,599
Let's go.

448
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:46,839
Mom, I'm heading out. Bye-bye.

449
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:01,640
Keep up!

450
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:03,000
Okay.

451
00:28:38,799 --> 00:28:39,799
Where did you find this?

452
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Over there.

453
00:28:44,759 --> 00:28:46,680
Here, drink some water.

454
00:28:56,680 --> 00:28:59,039
This kind of sound is
usually made during courtship

455
00:29:01,039 --> 00:29:02,160
to attract female birds.

456
00:29:03,359 --> 00:29:05,055
The more they attract,
the more excited they get,

457
00:29:05,079 --> 00:29:06,160
and the louder they call.

458
00:29:17,200 --> 00:29:18,680
It's like a pop star's concert.

459
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:21,216
The more enthusiastic the
applause from the audience,

460
00:29:21,240 --> 00:29:22,840
the more hyped the singer on stage gets.

461
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:33,440
Where are you going?

462
00:29:33,441 --> 00:29:34,759
I'm going ahead to take a look.

463
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:11,000
Qingtian!

464
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:56,799
Qingtian!

465
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:00,480
Qingtian!

466
00:31:02,039 --> 00:31:03,039
Qingtian!

467
00:31:04,480 --> 00:31:05,480
Qingtian!

468
00:31:06,440 --> 00:31:07,558
Mr. Xu,

469
00:31:07,559 --> 00:31:09,639
we need to find local
guides to go in right now.

470
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:10,599
A heavy fog is rolling in.

471
00:31:10,600 --> 00:31:13,359
We have to get out right now, Mr. Xu.

472
00:31:35,240 --> 00:31:36,639
None of you can go back in.

473
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:38,399
I called five more brothers
from the neighboring village.

474
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:40,400
Don't worry, we'll
definitely help you find him.

475
00:31:54,599 --> 00:31:56,200
I've already notified Changyang.

476
00:31:56,640 --> 00:31:57,880
He's on his way.

477
00:32:00,160 --> 00:32:02,039
Changyang knows where Qingtian might be.

478
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:38,399
Eight guides have already gone in,

479
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:39,600
and they haven't come out yet.

480
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:41,599
I'll go into the mountains, don't worry.

481
00:32:59,559 --> 00:33:01,919
Director Jiang, you guys head
back to the guesthouse first.

482
00:33:02,200 --> 00:33:03,400
We'll wait here.

483
00:33:10,279 --> 00:33:11,279
Mr. Xu.

484
00:33:18,599 --> 00:33:20,000
Go warm up by the fire for a bit.

485
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Let's go.

486
00:33:31,960 --> 00:33:33,240
I remember now.

487
00:33:33,759 --> 00:33:35,416
He said he was looking
for the Ghost Flower.

488
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:36,400
I'll go tell Changyang.

489
00:33:36,401 --> 00:33:37,761
He's looking for the Ghost Flower.

490
00:33:39,240 --> 00:33:40,278
He mentioned it in the car that day.

491
00:33:40,279 --> 00:33:41,039
Do you remember?
Wait until I go into the mountains,

492
00:33:41,680 --> 00:33:42,680
I'll find it for you.

493
00:33:43,200 --> 00:33:44,640
I know, Changyang knows.

494
00:33:52,640 --> 00:33:55,640
But if you find an injured
bird in the mountains,

495
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:56,960
do you send it away,

496
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:58,559
or return it to nature?

497
00:36:10,760 --> 00:36:12,640
Mom and Grandma are
arriving in Molie tomorrow.

498
00:36:13,159 --> 00:36:15,400
I'll send the most reliable
driver to pick them up.

499
00:36:17,039 --> 00:36:18,599
Let's make a secret pact.

500
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:23,199
We won't tell them Qingtian
passed away on the Great Snow Mountain.

501
00:36:25,960 --> 00:36:27,079
The journey is too far,

502
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:29,560
and the elderly can't
handle the exhaustion.

503
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:33,599
When I found Qingtian,

504
00:36:34,480 --> 00:36:36,760
I had already sent his soul back to Molie.

505
00:36:39,880 --> 00:36:41,639
What did you see in the forest?

506
00:36:48,599 --> 00:36:49,960
He belongs to the Great Snow Mountain.

507
00:36:52,400 --> 00:36:54,199
I don't want to hear this nonsense!

508
00:36:59,760 --> 00:37:01,199
What did you see?

509
00:37:04,480 --> 00:37:06,199
Who stopped you from bringing him out?

510
00:37:08,599 --> 00:37:09,599
Tell me!

511
00:37:12,239 --> 00:37:14,359
Just think of him as the
little prince of the forest.

512
00:37:15,760 --> 00:37:17,199
He left us a shoe,

513
00:37:17,599 --> 00:37:19,039
just to tell us

514
00:37:19,199 --> 00:37:20,399
he doesn't need shoes anymore.

515
00:37:21,599 --> 00:37:22,599
I want Qingtian!

516
00:37:25,559 --> 00:37:26,760
When you miss him,

517
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:29,599
just go back to the Great Snow Mountain.

518
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:34,559
I want Qingtian, that silly boy!

519
00:38:06,559 --> 00:38:08,159
Mom.

520
00:38:08,400 --> 00:38:09,400
You're in a good mood.

521
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:13,159
Grandma just showed me the sunrise.

522
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:15,960
Grandma showed me too.

523
00:38:17,079 --> 00:38:18,400
The old lady loves to show off.

524
00:38:20,559 --> 00:38:21,960
When are you coming back?

525
00:38:22,960 --> 00:38:23,999
It's been three months.

526
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:24,840
I haven't seen you.

527
00:38:24,841 --> 00:38:25,960
Mom misses you.

528
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:28,760
I'm not at home when
I'm at school either, right?

529
00:38:30,199 --> 00:38:31,559
How is that the same?

530
00:38:32,480 --> 00:38:34,239
Filming in the mountains is so dangerous.

531
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:36,198
What's dangerous about it?

532
00:38:36,199 --> 00:38:37,599
A bunch of my brothers are here.

533
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:39,000
Brother Wenshu is here too.

534
00:38:39,960 --> 00:38:41,599
Mom, I'm heading out.

535
00:38:42,639 --> 00:38:44,159
Go on. Stay safe.

536
00:38:44,840 --> 00:38:45,840
I'm leaving.

537
00:39:16,960 --> 00:39:20,800
Tiantian.

538
00:39:58,239 --> 00:40:00,480
Brother Wenshu, I found the Ghost Flower!

539
00:40:00,737 --> 00:40:01,776
I'll take a picture first,

540
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:02,639
and come find you in a bit
to bring you to see it.

541
00:40:30,960 --> 00:40:31,960
Boss.

542
00:40:32,400 --> 00:40:33,760
I have some dirt here.

543
00:40:34,159 --> 00:40:35,679
Can you pack it into a firework?

544
00:40:35,960 --> 00:40:37,080
I don't know how to do that.

545
00:40:37,199 --> 00:40:39,239
You can buy one and do it yourself.

546
00:40:41,280 --> 00:40:43,760
- Do you have phoenix fireworks?
- Expensive ones.

547
00:40:51,583 --> 00:40:53,776
[Phoenix's Call fireworks]

548
00:40:54,280 --> 00:40:55,440
Head back to the Great Snow Mountain.

549
00:41:16,076 --> 00:41:18,263
[From Changyang]

550
00:41:20,639 --> 00:41:22,000
Is it really that beautiful?

551
00:41:24,360 --> 00:41:25,360
Brother.

552
00:41:25,840 --> 00:41:27,360
Don't blame me for not telling you.

553
00:41:28,599 --> 00:41:30,399
Qinglang asked, and
I didn't tell him either.

554
00:41:32,199 --> 00:41:34,199
Being able to take this
photo and send it to you,

555
00:41:34,599 --> 00:41:35,760
I did my best.

556
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:39,679
I really can't describe it to you.

557
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:43,679
The fact that he left behind a clean shoe

558
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:46,239
is his way of telling us

559
00:41:46,599 --> 00:41:48,000
he's returned to the great forest.

560
00:41:49,079 --> 00:41:51,199
Let's just believe he belongs
to the Great Snow Mountain,

561
00:41:52,079 --> 00:41:53,599
and let him stay there.

562
00:42:05,239 --> 00:42:06,760
I read a book before.

563
00:42:07,760 --> 00:42:08,840
The author said,

564
00:42:10,159 --> 00:42:13,000
you can only see time after you die.

565
00:42:15,440 --> 00:42:16,599
When you're alive,

566
00:42:17,760 --> 00:42:19,199
time grows on you,

567
00:42:19,599 --> 00:42:20,800
so it's invisible.

568
00:42:23,079 --> 00:42:25,199
Growing up and growing old,

569
00:42:25,559 --> 00:42:27,199
isn't that seeing time?

570
00:42:27,559 --> 00:42:29,639
Those are just the
projections of time on a person,

571
00:42:30,400 --> 00:42:31,559
not time itself.

572
00:42:32,480 --> 00:42:33,760
When I die,

573
00:42:34,360 --> 00:42:36,160
and turn into a firework
flying into the sky,

574
00:42:36,239 --> 00:42:38,000
I'll be able to meet time face to face.

575
00:42:53,400 --> 00:42:54,776
Eating a few won't make you swell up.

576
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:56,360
I'll catch a few for you in the future.

577
00:42:58,679 --> 00:43:00,159
I've never walked this path either.

578
00:43:00,480 --> 00:43:02,040
Azha said a long time ago he'd take me.

579
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:03,679
He made it sound so mysterious.

580
00:43:04,239 --> 00:43:06,960
I thought I had to wait
for that person to appear,

581
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:08,239
so I could go with him.

582
00:43:09,719 --> 00:43:11,760
Xu Wenshu is stingy. I'll pay.

583
00:43:11,920 --> 00:43:13,640
We can't let anyone else live in our house.

584
00:43:13,960 --> 00:43:18,701
Furthermore: let's give names to all those
secret baces that we've been and haven't been to.

585
00:43:25,239 --> 00:43:27,239
Did you see it?

586
00:43:28,760 --> 00:43:31,199
That doesn't sound good. Pick another one.

587
00:43:47,279 --> 00:43:49,279
[Lucky because he
encountered the ghost flower]

588
00:43:54,666 --> 00:43:56,679
[Really wants to find the ghost flower]

589
00:44:03,339 --> 00:44:06,993
[To Changyang: I have a friend that really wants
to go into the forest to see the ghost flower]

590
00:44:07,017 --> 00:44:09,157
[I need you to watch over them.]

591
00:44:09,181 --> 00:44:13,054
[To Qingtian: My brother goes to the mountains
often, he can take you to find the ghost flower]
